# Who must approve a change, read by GitHub and GitLab from the repository root. The public kit names nobody: an
# organization's copy uncomments these lines with its own groups (GitLab: @group/subgroup; GitHub: @org/team), then
# turns on "require review from code owners" for the default branch. Without it, CODEOWNERS only suggests reviewers.
#
# What an agent reads at every session, and what runs on the workstations:
# /skills/            @your-org/ai-kit-maintainers
# /agents/            @your-org/ai-kit-maintainers
# /commands/          @your-org/ai-kit-maintainers
# /templates/         @your-org/ai-kit-maintainers
# /runtime/           @your-org/ai-kit-maintainers
# /organization.toml  @your-org/platform
# /practices/         @your-org/platform
#
# A contributed skill keeps its owner (skills/contrib/README.md):
# /skills/contrib/<name>/  @your-org/<owning-team>
#
# A team's own practices, reviewed by that team:
# /practices/20-<team>.md  @your-org/<team>
